1
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:05,440
Hello, everyone.

2
00:00:05,441 --> 00:00:07,079
Hello, Mr.Yang. Hi, everyone.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:08,480
Hello.

4
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:09,720
Mr.Yang, we meet again.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,799
Yesterday's exam is over.

6
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,359
And today we've reached

7
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,399
a new stage.

8
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,240
Today's lesson

9
00:00:15,241 --> 00:00:17,759
is mainly about emotion training.

10
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:18,320
And also,

11
00:00:18,321 --> 00:00:22,239
a little game about emotions for everyone.

12
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:23,000
But before

13
00:00:23,001 --> 00:00:24,719
the emotion game,

14
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,959
let's do a little bit of emotion training exercises first.

15
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:29,560
Okay?

16
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:29,720
Okay.

17
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:30,640
Talking about emotions,

18
00:00:30,641 --> 00:00:32,560
what kinds of emotions are there?

19
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,240
Joy, anger, sadness, happiness.

20
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,799
Fear.

21
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,480
Simply put,

22
00:00:36,481 --> 00:00:38,560
we can split emotions into two groups.

23
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:39,960
Positive and negative.

24
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,000
That's right.

25
00:00:41,001 --> 00:00:44,039
Emotions can be negative,

26
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:46,360
and they can also be positive.

27
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:49,200
Actually, there are special emotions too.

28
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,799
We'd like to invite two students

29
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,079
to improvise their take on

30
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:57,400
losing one's head in romance.

31
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:17,959
You're back.

32
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:19,559
Hey, have you had meals?

33
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,640
I'll go make you some food.

34
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:25,560
Here, sit down and eat.

35
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:28,959
I'm a bit tired.

36
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:29,999
I want to go rest first.

37
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,760
Are you thirsty?

38
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:32,280
No.

39
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:33,280
I'll get you some water.

40
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:35,880
Here, drink some water.

41
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,079
I want to sleep.

42
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:40,199
I'm tired, okay?

43
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,720
Let's just rest early today.

44
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:47,040
Then go ahead.

45
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,200
Okay.

46
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,520
You should rest early too.

47
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:55,640
You're back.

48
00:01:57,360 --> 00:01:58,560
What's going on?

49
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,960
Do you not love me anymore?

50
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:04,960
I think...

51
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,560
I'm just really tired, okay?

52
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:09,519
No...

53
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:11,680
Did I do something wrong?

54
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:15,559
I've already deleted every contact in my phone.

55
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,920
I only have you.

56
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,439
I think we both

57
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:19,840
need our own space.

58
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:22,119
I won't push you, okay?

59
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,520
Then what does that mean?

60
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:25,560
I'm just a little tired.

61
00:02:25,561 --> 00:02:27,440
So you want to break up, is that it?

62
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,160
I'll be honest with you.

63
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,360
I've never met anyone like you.

64
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:32,999
I think we're not right for each other.

65
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,319
I think I need some personal space.

66
00:02:35,320 --> 00:02:36,359
But you might

67
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,440
not really need personal space.

68
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:41,840
No...

69
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:44,240
Don't...

70
00:02:44,241 --> 00:02:51,239
Let's just call it quits, okay?

71
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,280
No, don't...

72
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,480
Don't come over here.

73
00:02:55,481 --> 00:02:56,800
I'm not coming over.

74
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,000
I'm just asking you one thing.

75
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,640
Do you love me?

76
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,559
No...

77
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,679
I don't have that...

78
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,839
Do you love me or not?

79
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,719
Fine, I do, okay?

80
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:10,680
Put the knife down first.

81
00:03:10,681 --> 00:03:12,039
Put the knife down, okay?

82
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:13,040
Put it down.

83
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:14,120
Put the knife down.

84
00:03:14,121 --> 00:03:16,200
That's not the answer I want.

85
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:19,840
Wang Ruijian.

86
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,200
Just give me one answer.

87
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,800
Do you love me or not?

88
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:25,760
I...

89
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,480
Three.

90
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,160
I love you.

91
00:03:29,161 --> 00:03:30,199
I love you, okay?

92
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:30,920
I'm begging you.

93
00:03:30,921 --> 00:03:32,320
Put the knife down.

94
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:36,080
Can you put the knife down?

95
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,679
Then promise me one thing.

96
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,640
Fine.

97
00:03:39,641 --> 00:03:40,799
What is it?

98
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,039
Just like me.

99
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,239
Delete every single contact

100
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:46,320
of the opposite sex from your phone.

101
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:48,320
Delete every last one.

102
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,280
No, wait.

103
00:03:56,281 --> 00:03:57,599
Do you even love me or not?

104
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,079
I do, I do love you, but...

105
00:03:59,080 --> 00:03:59,880
Then delete them right now.

106
00:03:59,881 --> 00:04:00,959
I'll delete, okay?

107
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,479
I'll delete.

108
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:03,320
Deleted. All deleted.

109
00:04:03,321 --> 00:04:05,000
Look, they're gone.

110
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:06,640
This one...

111
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,280
I knew you loved me.

112
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:14,720
Alright.

113
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:16,520
Okay, okay.

114
00:04:16,521 --> 00:04:17,679
Let's do a simple exercise.

115
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,039
But the main thing today

116
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,040
is to play this game.

117
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,399
This game is called

118
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,039
"Emotion Ranker".

119
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,719
The eight students will pair up

120
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,520
into four groups.

121
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,280
For each round,

122
00:04:26,281 --> 00:04:28,039
the four groups each draw

123
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,999
an Emotion Percentage card.

124
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,919
And based on the keywords I announce,

125
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,439
perform an improvisation.

126
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:34,519
After the performance,

127
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:36,439
each group must rank all four performances

128
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:38,959
from lowest to highest emotion value.

129
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,559
Groups that rank correctly get one point.

130
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:43,080
The top-scoring group at the end wins.

131
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:44,120
Then let's be a team.

132
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,040
We've never been on the same team.

133
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,000
We've never been.

134
00:04:46,001 --> 00:04:47,319
Come on.

135
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:47,880
Then us two.

136
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:48,840
Us two. Okay,

137
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:49,240
Sure.

138
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,040
Okay. Us two.

139
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,200
Come on.

140
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,400
Alright, you and I are a team.

141
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:57,040
The first round of the game is

142
00:04:58,760 --> 00:04:59,680
"a sense of brokenness".

143
00:04:59,681 --> 00:05:02,400
Each group sends one person to pick one.

144
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:16,159
Discuss based on the keyword

145
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:17,199
and the emotion percentage.

146
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,120
Sometimes,

147
00:05:18,121 --> 00:05:19,439
when one's broken to the extreme,

148
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:20,599
it's not just a tantrum anymore.

149
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:21,000
Right.

150
00:05:21,001 --> 00:05:22,079
He's become calm.

151
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:23,439
I think if I were playing this role,

152
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:24,999
I'd have to rely only on my eyes

153
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:25,800
and my feelings.

154
00:05:25,801 --> 00:05:27,599
Because brokenness is just a feeling.

155
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,280
You know what I mean?

156
00:05:28,281 --> 00:05:29,719
It's really just a feeling.

157
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,439
Someone who's broken doesn't talk much.

158
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,320
Personally, I think so.

159
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:33,000
I think so too.

160
00:05:33,001 --> 00:05:34,399
He just sits down quietly.

161
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:36,720
Actually, his heart has already truly shattered.

162
00:05:37,240 --> 00:05:38,160
A few words, but not many.

163
00:05:38,161 --> 00:05:40,401
So let me be the one to introduce what exactly happened.

164
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,080
Right.

165
00:05:41,081 --> 00:05:42,159
Sure, you just keep provoking me.

166
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,160
And I'm really withdrawn.

167
00:05:43,161 --> 00:05:44,240
Okay.

168
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:45,679
Too introverted. I have no friends.

169
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:47,439
Just like, the orphan type.

170
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,800
Alright, let's go, everyone.

171
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,400
Action.

172
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:56,160
Ziyu.

173
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,400
Hi, Zhixuan.

174
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,040
Today is my birthday.

175
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:01,040
Do you remember?

176
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,640
Your birthday?

177
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:06,280
Happy birthday.

178
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,560
This is the gift I want to give you.

179
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,080
This bear's been with me since childhood.

180
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:18,039
I'm leaving soon.

181
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,680
This is from this year's...

182
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:23,800
Why did you throw it away?

183
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:29,439
This has been with me since I was a kid.

184
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,760
I want to give it to you.

185
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:31,680
I know, fine, okay.

186
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,640
Just take this away.

187
00:06:32,641 --> 00:06:34,000
I'm busy with something.

188
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,560
Why?

189
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,960
Why would I celebrate your birthday?

190
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:40,119
You promised me.

191
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,239
What did I promise you?

192
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,240
Get out.

193
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:44,280
I'm going to play ball later, bye.

194
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,119
I told you to leave.

195
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,360
Can't you understand?

196
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:57,519
Is this the bear that's been with you since childhood?

197
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:58,520
Yes.

198
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:13,280
I can go now, right?

199
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,439
It can keep you company for me, Ziyu.

200
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:17,600
Who wants you to keep me company?

201
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,559
You think I'm the only one in class who plays with you,

202
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:22,119
so you're clinging to me now, aren't you?

203
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:24,520
Was it all fake, being with me all those years?

204
00:07:25,080 --> 00:07:26,856
Because I thought you looked pretty pitiful before.

205
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:29,161
No one else was willing to play with you and bullied you.

206
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,240
But today

207
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:33,599
I'm going to play basketball.

208
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,080
I just don't want to, so what?

209
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:37,960
Okay, that's enough.

210
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:38,960
I'm leaving.

211
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,800
My little bear.

212
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,000
Madam, he broke character, he gets fined.

213
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:51,800
Sorry.

214
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,199
You... yay.

215
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,200
What?

216
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,560
Damn it, yay.

217
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,840
Off you go.

218
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,520
Alright, second group.

219
00:08:58,760 --> 00:08:59,760
Brother.

220
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:04,840
It's been ninety-nine days since you left.

221
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,519
I don't know if you've

222
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:08,840
reunited with Mom in Heaven.

223
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:13,960
I remember a myth that says

224
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,759
on the hundredth day

225
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:17,920
a person reincarnates.

226
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,200
Will you reincarnate?

227
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,440
Will you go to

228
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:26,600
a new family, a new world?

229
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,880
Now I'm the only one left at home.

230
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,400
Honestly, I'm pretty lonely.

231
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,360
Mom passed away early.

232
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:48,519
We grew up together since we were little.

233
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:51,640
But why did even you have to leave me?

234
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:58,280
I don't know who to talk to.

235
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,920
I can only send you voice messages.

236
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,360
Ninety-nine of them.

237
00:10:03,361 --> 00:10:05,640
I've sent you ninety-nine voice messages.

238
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,479
I don't know what to do.

239
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,120
I don't know where to go.

240
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,240
I really miss you both so much.

241
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,040
But tomorrow is day one hundred.

242
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:31,480
I've decided

243
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:34,760
today is my last day sending you a voice message.

244
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:38,159
Once you get a good reincarnation tomorrow

245
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,480
and land in a good family,

246
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:40,999
once you start over

247
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,680
and live your new life,

248
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:47,200
I won't bother you anymore.

249
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,400
We'll just

250
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:55,800
each start

251
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,880
our own new lives.

252
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,079
One hundred percent.

253
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,560
It's fine.

254
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,839
Whose idea was this?

255
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,439
This came from a dream I had.

256
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:44,399
I dreamed I turned into a shadow.

257
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:45,320
In our performance class,

258
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:46,240
when this lesson came up,

259
00:11:46,241 --> 00:11:47,959
I came up with a bold idea and discussed it with Ruijian.

260
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,439
I said I once had a dream

261
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:51,639
that felt really broken.

262
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,479
Should we try putting it on stage?

263
00:11:53,480 --> 00:11:54,480
He said it's good.

264
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:55,759
So we tried it.

265
00:11:55,760 --> 00:11:57,159
But I truly came to feel

266
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:58,919
while performing on stage.

267
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:00,480
In the final part,

268
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:03,479
I chose reincarnation.

269
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:04,040
Because I felt

270
00:12:04,041 --> 00:12:06,081
truly staying behind, watching the people around me

271
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:10,039
grieve and suffer bit by bit

272
00:12:10,040 --> 00:12:11,359
and not being able to feel me anymore

273
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,599
is the most helpless thing of all.

274
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:15,479
I think we did pretty well.

275
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,880
We had this special chemistry.

276
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,760
Really impressive.

277
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,839
The Brokenness scene Ruijian and Guanyu performed...

278
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:26,119
I found it really moving.

279
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,159
It really touched me.

280
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:29,999
Coming up with something in such a short time

281
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,319
with such full emotions.

282
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:36,959
Characters and plot are such distinctive.

283
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,559
And one that moves the audience

284
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,919
and touches all of us.

285
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:42,080
I think it's amazing.

286
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,320
Group Three.

287
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:55,000
This is getting more and more absurd.

288
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:14,760
The singing girl knows not the sorrow of a fallen nation.

289
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:19,040
Across the river,

290
